<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 gold imports fall 48.8 pct--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 gold imports fall 48.8 pct--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports fell to 134.4 tonnes in 1996, down 48.8 percent from 262.3 tonnes the year before, according to data released on Monday by the Ministry of Finance.  </p>
<p>Market sources have said investor demand for gold fell sharply in Japan last year, in large part reflecting higher local prices due to the weaker yen.</p>
<p>This discouraged fresh buying while encouraging profit-taking by those who bought gold in 1995, a banner year for gold demand in which investor purchases were spurred by a strong yen, the Kobe earthquake and a series of banking crises.</p>
<p>Jewellery demand also slipped modestly last year, according to industry estimates.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
